(tangent blend between a lead-in/lead-out line and the toolpath's own)
(direction at the point where the pass actually starts or ends cutting -)
(replaces a sharp direction change with a smooth radius, to avoid a)
(velocity-direction shock at that corner)
(the toolpath-side point V is NOT displaced - trace_lathe always targets)
(it directly, so the arc must land exactly on it, tangent to fwd there;)
(only the lead line's own tangent point T1 is free to move)
(CALL vz[1] vx[2] fwd_cz[3] fwd_cx[4] lead_cz[5] lead_cx[6] radius[7] z_dir[8])
(fwd_cz/cx: unit vector, toolpath direction of travel at V, away from the arc)
(lead_cz/cx: unit vector, lead line direction, pointing from V's side toward)
(  the far rapid point, i.e. away from the cut - matching the existing)
(  li_ang/lo_ang convention already used to place that far point)
o<fillet_lead> sub

	#<_flt_ok> = 0
	o<flt_r0> if [#7 LE 0]
		o<fillet_lead> return
	o<flt_r0> endif

	(outward normal to the toolpath direction at V, same 90-degree rotation)
	(convention used for profile offsetting elsewhere in this codebase)
	#<_flt_nz> = [#8 * #4]
	#<_flt_nx> = [-#8 * #3]
	#<_flt_cz> = [#1 + #7 * #<_flt_nz>]
	#<_flt_cx> = [#2 + #7 * #<_flt_nx>]

	(tangent point on the lead line: same rotation applied to the lead)
	(direction, added from the center)
	#<_flt_t1z> = [#<_flt_cz> + #7 * #8 * #6]
	#<_flt_t1x> = [#<_flt_cx> - #7 * #8 * #5]

	(sweep sense from T1 to V: cross of r1,r2 GE 0 means the short way around)
	(is G3 CCW in this Z-X plane - verified numerically against rs274's own)
	(arc-endpoint radius check plus a rendered plot of the actual sweep)
	#<_flt_r1z> = [#<_flt_t1z> - #<_flt_cz>]
	#<_flt_r1x> = [#<_flt_t1x> - #<_flt_cx>]
	#<_flt_r2z> = [#1 - #<_flt_cz>]
	#<_flt_r2x> = [#2 - #<_flt_cx>]
	#<_flt_cross> = [#<_flt_r1z> * #<_flt_r2x> - #<_flt_r1x> * #<_flt_r2z>]
	o<flt_cw> if [#<_flt_cross> GE 0]
		#<_flt_cw> = 0
	o<flt_cw> else
		#<_flt_cw> = 1
	o<flt_cw> endif

	#<_flt_ok> = 1

o<fillet_lead> endsub
